Peter LANGSTOEGER wrote:

> In article <37C9FDAD.E75D3A61@sprint.ca>, RouterSlayer <routerslayer@sprint.ca> writes:
> >1. can you use ANY hard drive with a vaxstation (3100 M76) or DEC alpha
> >(3000-300lx) or just DEC?
>
> You should be able to use any SCSI compliant device.
> As there is no such "SCSI compliancy" YMMV.
>
> >2. whats the maximum size of hard drive, 2gigs, or more?
>
> Depends on what to do with the disk. VAXstation 3100 have only 6Byte
> SCSI Init Commands in (EP)ROM, so the max. size of a system disk is ~1GB
> (unless you want to reprogram some MoBo chips - which some already did).
> And what the max. size of a data disk is, depends on the opsys and the
> version of the opsys.
>
> >3. how do you partition and format a new (fresh from the store) drive
> >for these systems?
>
> Depends on the opsys. Partitioning is not a word used with OpenVMS.
>
> (Low Level) Formating is (if ever) part of the console code
>         (eg. TEST 75 in the VS3100 for hard disks, TEST 70 for floppy)
>         and initing a filesystem on the disk depends on the opsys.
>
> >4. how do you do it if you're replacing the main system drive and not
> >just adding storage? (ie, how to do #3 for augmenting storage - adding a
> >drive and how to do #3 if it's replacing the main system drive) ?
>
> Depends on the opsys. With OpenVMS a BACKUP/IMAGE is sufficient.
>
> Without more infos you won't get sufficient help.
>
> Check out       http://www.openvms.digital.com/wizard/openvms_faq.html
