net wrote:
> 
> Hello,
> 
> I have a tape stuck in the TK70 unit of my microvax 3300. For some
> reason it can't find the boot information on the tape and I can't remove
> it.
> Is there a way from the console to issue commands to the TK70 to make it
> rewind the tape so I can remove it?
> 
> Thanks,
> 
> MArcio
 Ah. Sometimes happens.

I would switch off the system, slide out/unscrew the tape drive
(may need to undo a lot of screws etc), pull the drive out so you can
get to/see the take up reel (internal).

power on your system (power applied to drive) and use a CLEAN finger to
wiggle the take up reel, push it CLOCKWISE  as viewed from the
top, and you may just free it.

i did the other day when i had a tk70 stuck..... i felt a click and it
started to unload the tape. I was lucky and the power lead was long
enough and I balanced it on a chair in front of the system.

HTH, Nic.



