Marcio,

The problem may be due to the tape itself. Some old TK70 and TK50 tapes
will stick like glue to the head. If can free the tape, check to see if
there is a hole in the circuit board under the drive. At least a TZ86
drive has one. If so, you can use a screw driver to turn the take-up
motor to rewind the tape to a point where the drive will rewind when
powered on.

If you get the tape out, throw it away. The next problem is that the
stuck tape may have left something on the head. Run a cleaning carridge
before doing anything else.

We have some special 0.5 inch non-shedding fabric that we use to wet
clean DLT drives with IPA after experiencing stuck tapes. However, this
requires disassembly of the drive further than you may wish to go.

Good luck.

Bill

