Reeve McGinniss wrote in message <37c86752.4350465@news.uswest.net>...
>I'm looking for the specs on an old TZ30 DLT tape drive. Failing that,
>perhaps a pointer to a site with the info.


The TZ30 is a 1/2 high tape drive that uses either CompacTape or CompacTape
II cartridges.

It is not a DLT drive.

It records 95 MB on tape.  It is basically a smaller version of a SCSI TK50
drive.

It can not read higher density tapes.  It can not reuse tapes that have been
written on by a higher density tapes.

-John





