Reeve McGinniss wrote:
> 
> I'm looking for the specs on an old TZ30 DLT tape drive. Failing that,
> perhaps a pointer to a site with the info.

It's a 5.25" half-height drive, SCSI interface, that reads and
writes TK50 ("CompacTape") cartridges.  These cartridges were
widely used from the mid-80's to the early 90's on DEC
PDP-11's and VAXen for software distribution and system backup,
and are still used (to a lesser extent) today.  Capacity is
nominally 70 Mbytes.  Typical time to read or write all 70 Mbytes
is most of an hour.

If you have any media conversion needs involving TK50's (or other
DEC media), feel free to contact me.

