In article <7q1shd$4fn$1@news.ccit.arizona.edu>,
Gordon C Zaft  <zaft@u.arizona.edu> wrote:
>Jerry Ryan - Lab IT - 733-3595 <ryan@horta.mmm.com> wrote:
>> I recently acquired a VAXStation 4000 VLC (with no documentation, of course!)
>
>> During the power up test it produces the message
>> ?54 Retry
>> and appears to hang
>
>> What is the translation of this message?
>
>	Generally, it means the machine couldn't find any boot files on 
>whatever device it's trying to boot from.  
>

  It probably means it's trying to boot off the Ethernet and there's no
bootserver for it.  If you push the halt button on the side of the machine
and do a "SHOW BOOT" you'll see that it's trying to boot from device ESA0:.
It probably was used as a satillite node in a cluster.  A "SHOW DEVICE" will
let you know if you've got an internal disk drive.  Try setting the boot
device to the internal disk, "SET BOOT DKA100", for example and then "BOOT"
and see if there's an operating system on the internal disk.  If not you'll
either have to install one or use a VMScluster that you can boot into.

--
