A. Khan (khan@saab21.freeserve.co.uk) wrote:
: Hi... sorry if this is the wrong newsgroup for this but i cant find info
: anywhere!!...
: 
: Basically i have acquired a Digital LN03 Plus laser printer (old
: printer).... It is a serial port printer. I need help with the cable. Does
: anyone know anyhting about this printer? Does it use a standard serial to
: serial cable, or special wired??
: Any help would be appreciated...(An emailed response would be much
: appreciated as i dont use NG much!)..

The serial port on the LN03 is wired DTE, like all Data Terminal Equipment
should be.

If you connect it to a DCE equipment (a modem), you use a straight-thru cable.

If you connect it to another DTE equipment (like a PC or a computer), you use
a null modem cable. 

A null modem cable is one which has female connectors on each end, and pins 2
and 3 are swapped internally.  Additional pins may also be swapped, such as
having pin 20 on one end connected to pins 6 and 8 on the other end, and vice
versa.

        Stu



