Anybody familiar with the evolution of this product?  I had found a
P5c133 for the Starion frankenclone I was reviving.  While comparing the
contents of the scrap screw jar to the Motherboard mounting posts thread
size I noticed a set of unused pins.  Or, at anyrate a set of pins I had
not found a use for.

These unused pins (4 pin block) are labeled as HDD active display on the
MB.  They are in excess of the standard HDD light on the chassis case
front

I have no plans to employ the second IDE channel with anything other
than a CD drive.  It is just a point of curiosity as to how Hard drive
activity other than the more normal simple activity LED would have been
used?




