>
> 1- Alpha still has quite a technological edge so it  will continue to exist.
> People have been predicting the death of the PPC chip forever, yet it is still
> alive and keeping up.

The market for Alpha, then, will be limited to Linux, Tru64 and OpenVMS. Since
Compaq's marketing of _ALL_ of its non-Intel lines remains as abysmal as Digital's
ever was, maybe worse, the future is dubious, at best.

> 2- Compaq probably realised that Microsoft wasn't all that interested in 64
> bit Alphas. Might as well drop support for it. (considering that sales weren't
> all that high).

Rather ironic as outside of the IA64 emulators and such out there, there is no
