Over the past 12 years, I have watched a lot of management at various levels
within Digital and now Compaq make decisions. Decisions have been made with
knowledge, without knowledge, out of spite, playing games, for all kinds of
reasons, both good and bad. I have seen all kinds of good decisions and many
bad decisions. Once Ken Olsen was let go, most decisions made were bad.
things like laying off staff to make the corporation profitable. Closing
facilities because that's what the Wall Street money mavens wanted.
Purchasing huge quantities of memory just before the price of memory took a
nose dive and thus causing a loss of hundreds of millions of dollars. Hiring
various people without vision, just because they could say PeeCee, or
Windows, or OS/2 or Next. We did Contract manufacturing and this was both
good and bad. Good cause we made use of idle and expensive macinery, bad
because Apple used to use this process to figure out if they're costs to
build were in line with ours.
We got into the PC business and out and in and outand in again and then the
LapTop business and out and in and out and in again. We purchased a large
number of PeeCee Laptops from an Italian firm and they all had the Digital
brand Name on them and they were crap. We had to buy back hundreds of
thousands of these and trash them. But we had a contract with that firm,
signed and solid with Enrico Pessatori who worked for them and so we ended
up having to buy desktop systems from those people in Italy, the ones that
made those miserable LapTops to fullfill the agreement. But the people who
used to build the product here didn't like them cause they had lot's of
sharp metal edges and design wise they had too many screws and they took so
long to build. Then Enrico started to Work for Digtial. Well, Enrico works
for Compaq and it is he who has made this great decision to cease NT on
Alpha. Not Compaq, not Microsoft, Enrico. Why I don't know, but I think this
is another bad decision and that the correct decision should have been to
get someone with Vision to run Compaq.

There are thousands, maybe hundreds of thousands of Windows NT only Alpha's
out there.
These machines will only run Windows NT for one or more of the following
three reasons.
1. A fusible link on the CPU chip has been blown, to knock out OpenVMS or
Digital UNIX capability.
2. The SROM, has been modified and will not generate a HWPRB, so OpenVMS and
UNIX cannot identify the hardware type and thus will not install nor run.
3. No SRM was created for the platform.

Any one with one of these artificialy inhibited machines should be damn
pissed off about this decision and should hound Compaq about getting
replacement hardware.

rtt





