The older DECpc LPx did not contain a flash BIOS. The .bin file is the hex
file used by a PROM burner to create a BIOS chip. Services has BIOS chips
that are pre-burned with the hex file - you can order them by part number.

The newer DEC PCs used a flash PROM device that allows you to upgrade
the BIOS chip. This uses the Phoenix phlash utility. For those BIOS' that
have newer versions, there will be a self-extracting file that will create
an
update disk or there will be a ZIP file that you will have to copy to a
bootable
diskette.

Hope this helps,

glen kelley
compaq

