>>w/ no O/S, and  No-O/S (presumeably Linux/NetBSD..) won handily?

  Please don't assume that alphas bought without OS are running Linux
   Those of us in education buy alphas without OS and the appropriate
    VMS or TRU64 BASE license (and DECW Motif for VMS).  Everything
    else is in the Campus License program.  So for us it is cheaper to
    buy an alpha with no OS and add a base license to run VMS and/or TRU64
     than to buy a packages VMS or Unix Alpha.

    So all machines bought without OS are not necessarily running Linux
    Using the Alpha/No-OS numbers to establish Linux use is incorrect
    Some of those machines  are running VMS and TRU64 

