hbligth@ge.com.nospaem (Harry Bligth) wrote:

>Who knows what "Tru64 UNIX" is outside of Q? Seems that part of Option is out.

I went to a campus "Unix Fair" on Tuesday. Presentations included:

Linux by campus IT people, all on Dell systems which is what they sell
and support

AIX on RS6000 by IBM's top RS6000 guy. Very strong push, much talk of
discounts and grants

Solaris on Sun (and Intel) by strong Sun team. Much talk of discounts.

Mac OS X by Apple people.

No Compaq presence. No mention of Alpha. No mention of Tru64 UNIX.

Campus support for VMS is waning fast and systems are being shut down.
I do not even know if we have a Compaq/Digital sales person. We used
to be a major VAX/VMS site. The beginning of the end was Digital's
push into the commercial market in the mid 80s, which seemed to
require abandoning the academic market and created a splendid
opportunity for Sun.

I recently shut down an Alpha NT server because of the difficulty of
getting printer drivers (it was only doing file/print serving). It
will probably be revived as a Linux box, though a cheap VMS
migration might be attractive.

