Dear friends,

I got a MicroVax 3300 from a old computer store and I'm trying to make
the system work again.
When it starts it begins the normal tests and then a countdown that
stops at 3 (only 3 to go before it pass all the tests).
Then I get: "Normal operation not possible" and the console prompt.
If I do a SHOW DSSI it gives:

DSSI Node 7 (*)

But it doesn't list any of the two internal DISKs.
With a SHOW DEVICE it lists the TK70, as MUA0, but I don't have a boot
tape to try it.
I have searched the Internet for specifc information about this
hardware, but I couldn't find much.
It has become a challenge to bring this machine back to live. I have
started a mini-network of people I know have worked with VAXen before,
to try to revive the system. I even got a technician from Compaq
(Digital support) to find me a console cable with a DB-9 connector to
connect the serial port to a notebook (for free!).
This machine is very dear to me, that's why I need someone to help.

Please, any help is very welcomed.

Thanks,

Marcio Pocciotti




