In article <fgxlmj.155@inter.NL.net>, Richard van den Berg <ravdberg@inter.NL.net> writes:

|> The "DEC 3000 300/400/500/600/700/800/900 AXP Models System Programmer's
|> Manual" is also available at http://decstation.unix-ag.org/

There is/was also a pointer to the same document off the NEtBSD/alpha web
pages.

|> And all other prom console commands and tests. BTW in which other
|> document are SIR and SIMR for the MAXine covered?

AFAIK there has never been a publically-available document which completely
describes the 3MIN, MAXINE, or 3MAXPLUS hardware. The people who did the
4.4bsd/pmax had access to the relevant hardware definitions from DEC
sources.  Many of the bits of them are the same as the corresponding bits
in the ioctl asic used in TC Alphas (see the junkio chapter of the.  The
SCSI control is unique to DECstations, and the interrupt mapping is
different on each model.

You could figure it all out from looking at the NetBSD (or 4.4bsd/pmax)
headerfiles: that's how I did it.

Jonathan Stone -- pure personal opinion, not speaking for COMPAQ.



