You can probably upgrade the processor to at least an Intel 80486-DX4
5v(!) OverDrive processor without any BIOS upgrade or other hardware
changes.

Let me know the exact DEC part number of the motherboard, and I'll be
able to determine whether or not a Pentium-class processor card is
possible.  The DEC part number is either 54-nnnnn for the finished
board with components mounted on it or 50-nnnnn for the bare board.
Look for the part number silk-screened (etched) along the edge of the
board as part of the process of etching the circuits onto the board.
The part number is NOT printed on a sticker.  The info displayed by
the motherboard BIOS also identifies the motherboard, tho not quite as
precisely.

With the right main logic board, a Pentium-level upgrade may work.

... Ben 

