I'd like it better if it were not for the statement which follows
it:

   Our OpenVMS strategy has four key elements. 

   We will continue to focus on solutions for customers in SELECT
   TARGET MARKETS. 

   Outside of these target markets, WE WILL PROVIDE AN EASY MIGRATION PATH TO
   COMPAQ TRU64 UNIX AND WINDOWS NT for those customers who want to migrate.
   This supports our goal of keeping OpenVMS customers as Compaq customers. 

    (capitalization mine)

  This suggests that if you are not in one of the Compaq defined "select
target markets" ( whatever those might be ), they have no interest in
keeping you as a VMS customer but will be quite happy to sell you a Unix
or NT solution to replace it with. They still haven't gotten the message
that this isn't what we want.

   As I've said before, if (when?) I'm forced by Compaq to abandon VMS
because I'm not the sort of VMS customer they want I'll do everything
in my power to make sure the replacement system has no Compaq content
whatsoever.

