 Using a Dec Xp1000 ( DUnix 4.0e ) and the PowerStorm 300 graphic
card.

 We have problems with our software that uses the X11 Shared
memory extensions and the shared memory pixmaps, it seems that 
the Xserver does not support the shared memory pixmaps.

when using a test program that calls XShmQueryExtenstion everything
is OK, but when I call XShmQueryVersion, the function returns that
I don't have the Shared memory pixmaps. ( the last parameter of 
the XShmQueryVersion ).

 On an older AlphaStation 250 4/266 ( DUnix 4.0e ), the same program
reports that I have access to Shared pixmaps. this is an older
machine.

 The questions are : can it be possible that a particular 
graphic card ( PowerStorm 300 ) does not support Shared pixmap ? 
or is it only the XServer that does not ?

 Is there any configuration switches that I have to do to 
configure the XServer so it can support the shared pixmaps ?

 I have some difficulty in understanding why ( if it's the case) a
more recent hardware can't support shared pixmaps ? is it that it's
not
fast enough ?

 anyway, 

 Thanks for any informations or hints.

	Max.


P.S. here's the small test program to see if I have access to 
shared pixmaps:


/********** test program **************/
/* cc test.c -o test -lXext -lX11     */

#include <stdio.h>
#include <X11/Xlib.h>


/*XTestQueryExtension*/

int main ( int argc, char** argv)
{

  Display *dpy;
  int minor;
  int major;
  int pixmap;
  int status;

  dpy = XOpenDisplay(":0.0");

  if (!dpy)
  {
    printf("no Display\n");
    return -1;
  }

  status = XShmQueryExtension(dpy );
  
  printf( " status : %i\n", status );
  status =  XShmQueryVersion(dpy, &major,  &minor, &pixmap );

  printf( " status : %i\n", status );
  printf( " major : %i\n", major );
  printf( " minor : %i\n", minor );
  printf( " pixmap : %i\n", pixmap );

  return 1;

}


 
