Newsgroups: comp.sys.dec

$ prog :== $mydirectory:myprog.exe
$ prog -1 -2 -3

The dollar sign in column 1 is the standard OpenVMS prompt.

The dollar sign in string equate will translate into run myprog.exe, but
unless you specify your directory or the actual location of your executable,
the system will default to running myprog.exe in sys$system.

The second line is of course, the actual run of your program, with it's
parameters and you should be able to pick them up with argc and argv.

rtt





