I have three DEC RZ28 drives, and luckily I have found jumper settings
for them - except for one jumper. 

Take a look at http://www.pc-disk.de/pcdisk/h/LAYOUT/246.HTM .

This is what the PCBs look like, BUT: Two of my disks have a 2pin header
connector relatively close to the corner diagonally opposite the power
connector (2-3 cm towards the Termination Header). One of them has a
jumper placed, not the other one.
The third drive does not have this header soldered in, leaving empty
holes in the pcb.
I have searched and searched the 'net for any information about this
jumper, I even mailed some authors of previous postings. No luck so far.
Oh - they answered, but didn't know about it.

Please tell me if you have any idea...

