Greetings.
I have had a DEC Starion 942 in the garage that some people were tossing
out.  The p5 133, cache chips, simms, video memory, drives and all
screws holding it together were gutted out.

So, it pretty much is a Main board, back plane card, case, and power
supply.  I had not yet fired off the power supply to see if it was any
good.

Is there any Junque dealers that  specialize in DEC stuff?  I will
probably need the cover plates that decorate the 5.25 bays.  I am at
this moment downloading some info files from support for information on
what the Cache chips were, and video ram extra meg.  Those I assume are
the $5.00 Ram "chiclets" all the local purveyors of old crap have laying
about.

I have no clue on the cache chips?  Nuts and bolts are simple enough.
They did also toss the Starion restore CD and a 1.44 floppy along with a
pretty (useless) users guide.

I am torn between, returning this Starion 942 to service for my Niece to
use as a collegiate workhorse or to just pick up a generic 133 system
clone locally.

Anyway, thats my two cents worth of input to the news group.  Should
some soul have some odds and ends.  Drop me a line.

Richard W. Ramo
RWRamo@Hotmail.com




