Richard,

You can download the Starion 900 series service maintenance manual
from...

http://www4.service.digital.com/documentation/pcdoc/star920.htm

at least until Compaq decides to change the URL again to make this
info hard to find.  One positive fact is the DEC/Compaq state that the
Starion 900 BIOS is Y2K-compliant.

The Starion uses a riser card setup like a lot of NEC, HP, IBM, and PB
computers, but it is otherwise a pretty standard setup.  

As far as I'm concerned, it all depends on how much work and money you
have to invest in rehabbing the box.  If the motherboard and power
supply are good, it may well be worth it.  You can get away without
upgrading video memory and/or cache memory to save a few bucks.  The
video memory upgrade consists of a pair of standard off-the-shelf
256Kx16 video DRAMS, nothing special, but 1MB of video memory is
enough to get by... Ben Myers

