> memory subsystem for the UP2000?

It's a dumbed-down version of the DP264 subsystem.

From Shannon Knows Compaq V6N19, July 9, 1999:

Debuting with Slot B was the UP (as in Ultimate Performance) 2000, a
dual-processor-capable Alpha motherboard based on an extended ATX form
factor. The UP2000 supports one or two Alpha Slot B processors starting
at 667MHz, and uses the same Compaq 21272 Tsunami core logic chipset
found on Compaq�s DP264 motherboard. In its role as a cost-reduced
variant of the DP264, the UP2000 sells for about $1.2K less than
equivalent DP264 offerings, but is constrained by slower memory and a
maximum memory capacity of 2GB compared with 4GB.

