The Venturis FX service maintenance manual states the following.

� Memory - At least 8 MB of EDO DRAM standard, expandable up to
192 MB using 32 MB SIMMs. For Venturis FXe models, at least 8 MB of
EDO DRAM standard, expandable up to 128 MB using 32 MB SIMMs

54-21225-JA	1MX32 60 ns EDO DRAM Module (4MB EDO)
54-21246-JA	2MX32 60 ns EDO DRAM Module (8MB EDO)
54-23170-HA	4MX32 60 ns EDO DRAM Module (16MB EDO)
54-21277-KA	8MX32 60 ns EDO DRAM Module (32MB EDO)

As far as I know, the DEC SIMMs are vanilla generic EDO non-parity.  I
have used them interchangably on DEC Venturis FX and other systems
with Intel-made motherboards, which set the standard for SIMM memory.

I suspect that you have some defective SIMMs there.  One other
possibility is that the external cache module may be defective.  Try
removing the module or disabling external cache in the system CMOS
setup.

Memory must be installed in matched pairs in Venturis FX systems,
pretty much like all other Pentium systems.  The systems also work
properly with fast page mode SIMMs.

In the future, you're better off posting any personal computer related
questions to comp.sys.dec .  A friend forwarded your posting to me via
email.

.. Ben Myers

