reid@psi.ch (Dr Ivan D Reid, muSR Facility) writes:

> 	What's the theoretical maximum integer/FP instructions per clock
> cycle for the EV67?

IIRC, it can issue four, start executing six, and retire eight instructions
per cycle. There are two integer clusters with two functional units each,
and two fp functional units. There are complicated rules that govern issue
of instructions. See the compiler writers guide available somewhere on the
web (it's a shame that downloaded files can't remember the URL they came
from...).

