Ray,

Jumper settings are specific to the model of drive, DEC or otherwise.
Look on the surface of the drive circuit board for tiny etched fine
print describing the jumpers.

The EASIEST way to use older DEC SCSI drives on a PC is by connecting
them to a SCSI host adapter with a BIOS setup parameter to trigger the
drives to spin up.  Many, but not all, older DEC drives do not spin up
when power is applied, the way PC (and most newer) SCSI drives do.
Instead, they have to receive a SCSI spin up command from the host to
start spinning and running... Ben Myers 

