>
>	I have a DEC 3000/600 Alpha box, 21064 series CPU. Does anyone happen
>to know what the command is, from the console, to do a low-level format on
>a given hard drive?

I don't think there is such a command on this system.

However, on a TOTALLY UNSUPPORTED basis, there is a program
supplied with VMS in the SYS$ETC directory (SYS$ETC is a
logical name) that lets you do things to SCSI devices.
It's called RZTOOLS_ALPHA.EXE and it has some built-in
help.

Please keep in mind that tools that directly manipulate
hardware devices, especially SCSI, can be used to put the
device into a non-working and unrecoverable state if you
do something wrong.

This directory also contains a utility that lets you examine
device mode pages (generally safe, if all you do is look),
and utilities for updating the firmware in a number of
drives.

