More like <= 0.05% (200-500ppm) in my experience, though it depends on
the capacitive loading in the series configuration. I've seen one
semi-pro DAT recorder built that way! 

But I agree, a helluva big number compared with the basic accuracy of a
cheap crystal - 20-30ppm typical, 50ppm should be a wildly conservative
estimate of drift over lifetime. 

I've seen 2-3ppm drift after about a year in a thermal test oven. 
And (from memory) about 10ppm overnight at 160 celsius. (Damn oven. 
How was *I* to know that "SP 60" meant 60% power, not 60 celsius? :-)


