Make sure that you have that piece of LMF licence paper for Open3D as well
otherwise the whole machine will freeze when you try to run any OpenGL
apps. You will then have to telnet in from another machine and kill the X
server. 

Our supplier, non other than what was then Digital Singapore, did not give
us those papers and our machines were basically high-tech paper weights. I
spent the next 2 weeks frantically logging error calls with our ISVs and
searching the then-Digital web pages before realizing what was going on. I
then had to explain to the sales manager about their own products and it
still took him a quite a few days to consult his colleagues before finally
getting us those licence papers.

Stephen Wong
