>Hmmm... now what is so great about Storageworks ??/

Eg. The bricks concepts. With a box, taking up 5 1/4 disks, 3 1/2 disks,
DLT tapes, DAT tapes, and so on. Selecting one or two busses in the box
by a jumper. Selecting SCSI address by the slot#. Selecting host address by
using the id of the power supply slot...

Problems came in with the SCSI-2 16bit (disk supported it, but not the
controllers), the SCSI-3 and finally with the low profile disks.

StorageWorks was (is ?) a great concept. It seems, it simple stopped evolution.
And now we seem to have a revolution...

