standards across their platforms. Add to this the onset of LVD, FC drives,
and disks spinning in excess of 14K RPM. Simply, StorageWorks I (for lack of
a better term) has outlived its usefulness. The heat, vibration, and EMI gen
erated by the new drives forces a new packaging system.

SW II is a next generation of power & packaging. More disks will fit in the
same footprint. The same disk unit will be usable across all three
platforms.

Sounds like you need to grab your CPQ salesrep, and have a serious
Non-Disclosure around StorageWorks.

