The accuracy of the crystals is better than 1% without having to 
resort to ovens. There is a rather large "error" in the frequency
sysnthesis, however. PC's (since the original PC) derive their 
clock from a 14.318MHz crystal. The system frequency is a 
rational number multiple of 14.318MHz. To get to 133MHz (which I 
assume the processor from hell would have) one might multiply by 
28/3 which gets us to 133.63MHz. The processor would then run at 
668.17MHz. I think that could safely get past the tripple-6. ;-)

