I think that the Venturis BIOS is smart enough to detect a video card
and disable the on-board video.  Never tried it, tho.  That's the way
most well-designed motherboards with integrated video seem to work.
The Venturis desktops are decent designs.

>What type of sound cards work with this model?

Follow the straight and narrow and use a well-recognized name brand
sound card, not a cheap one.  Because DEC themselves offered the
Creative Labs Sound Blaster cards, I recommend one of these.

>What type of disk drives work with this model?

Commodity IDE drives.

>I have not found any information in the Service
>manual on the features of the disk controller.
>Is it just plain IDE or is it much better?

"Plain IDE" is the original IDE, up to only 528 MB.  Your Venturis
BIOS supports up to at least 2.1GB, maybe 8.4GB.  I'm not sure,
because I don't have enough hours in the day to test all these
possibilities.  The BIOS also accepts and recognizes standard
off-the-shelf ATAPI/EIDE CD-ROM drives... Ben Myers

