Hummm, Hello all:

Well, I can't agree with that.  When starting up NT (Server or Workstation)
from a fresh (clean) disk larger than 4GB you are right.  However, the
limitation is 4GB.  This is due to NT formatting in FAT16 vs. NTFS.  Of
course any partition you create after that you can format however you wish,
provided you have the proper BIOS and SP to support larger than 8.4GB.

But, if you preformat the drive using NTFS prior to the install, it will
most definitely work.

In the case of the original poster, I believe the problem was that drive "C"
for formatted FAT32 and therefore NT could not "recognize" the boot drive
partition.  Since it must place the boot files there no matter where
x:\winnt\ resides.


Respectfully:

Clifford W. Owen
