>   21264A    667     37.5        33.3          65.5       53.9
>   21264     500     26.9        23.2          52.2       44.5
> 
>   Ratio    1.33     1.39        1.43          1.25       1.21
> 
> The integer performance of the 21264A has increased supralinearly
> with respect to clock rate, especially for the base score. 

The primary reason is software.  We're using a newer version of 
the compiler with a newer code generator, and we've improved the 
tuning. (I'm sure of this; I am the engineer who built the SPEC 
CPU95 binaries used here.)

There may also be some latency tweaks in the memory system (but 
I'm not sure on that point, since somebody else actually did the 
runs on the XP1000.)

No new instructions were used in the SPEC submission; note that
the submission says '-arch ev6'.  Nor were there any occult 
contributions based on the proximity to a beastly number, to the
best of my knowledge.

