Now, I'm the first to answer my own questions.

>1) The DECserver 90M boots from internal flash and after a few seconds
>is ready (message: Image loaded). Then it sits there for some minutes (!!)
>and does nothing. After this (message: software initialized) the server
>is accepting connections.
>
>OpenVMS wizards thinks it is decompressing the image. I can't believe this.
>I think, it is looking for an IP address via BOOTP/TFTP frames on the net.
>Does anyone has more insight ? 

If MNENG2 (the compressed image) is loaded, then decompression occurs
on boot time. It is said to take 5 min.
If MNENG3 (the uncompressed image) is loaded, then the minutes delay are
not caused by image decompression (of course).

And my server has the MNENG3 loaded...

>                                Will this time shorten, after I configured
>the server (NVRAM) ?

We'll see...

>Why is the 90M doing this ? The 90TL (if not configured, too) inits after
>seconds and is reachable via MOP (but of course needs a config for TELNET).
>A 90M is not reachable via MOP during the minutes of initializing.

Still no clue.

>2) The DECserver 90M has a UTP Ethernet Port on the front-panel. it should
>work just like the BNC Ethernet Port on the side or the DEChub Backpanel
>Ethernet Connection on the rear. In fact it is not.
>
>After SW init completion, the network connection via backplane and
>BNC is working, via UTP it does not work. On the hub supplying the UTP
>connection to the DECserver the link LED is lite during 90M software
>loading and initializing, but goes off when init completes !
>
>Does anyone know a reason ? Is there a Config parameter needed to
>enable the UTP port ?

I forgot to mention, that I tried this with a Stackable Unit, because this
was the first power supply I found in my department store.

If a DECserver 90M is used in the Stackable Shelf but standalone (no
other stackable units attached and therefore BNC not in use) the
Position Identifier Dial must be switched to the Agent position.

The UTP port on my DS90M is now working properly.

>3) MNENG1 is the image for the DECserver 90TL (currently V1.1C, old,
>no access server functions). MNENG2/MNENG3 is for the 90M (currently
>V2.3A, current, access server functions called "Network Access SW")
>What is the difference between MNENG2 (mentioned in manual) and
>MNENG3 (loaded in the DECserver 90M) ?

MNENG2 and MNENG3 are the same software. MNENG2 is compressed to fit
in 1MB flash. MNENG3 is not compressed, requires more than 1MB flash (=>2MB)
and it useful for saving the time of decompression (5 minutes !!)

MNENG2/MNENG3 are not only for the DS90M, they are also for the 4MB RAM
version of the DS90TL (which is AFAIK not very common).

>The "Network Access SW" for the DECserver 900TM, we also have, is called
>WWENG2 (and I think but don't know, there is a WWENG1 for a DECserver 700)
>
>
>4) Does anyone have a "reset" file for the 90M ? Is one supplied in TSM ?

A reset file is not supplied with TSM but is supplied (in fact more than one)
with the DNAS software package _for_ the TSM.

>5) How to update the software in flash ?
>I know how to boot from flash or from the network (MOP or BOOTP/TFTP) but
>I still have no clue, how to update the image in the flash if needed.

Anyone ?


6) What is the part# of a 4MB Memory upgrade for a DS90TL ?
If it has a reasonable price, maybe we upgrade all our DS90TL, just to
use the same software (DNAS) on all DS90.
